# Testing Rules

- Unit/integration tests: `tests/test_*.py` with shared fixtures in `tests/conftest.py`.
- `pytest-asyncio` is `asyncio_mode = auto` — prefer async tests for DB/HTTP paths.
- Prefer focused tests that lock behavior at stage/module boundaries over huge end-to-end only suites.
- Decision-detection quality: `eval/harness.py` + labeled dataset — update when changing Stage 1/2 recall/precision tradeoffs.
- Do not commit real Discord/GitHub payloads containing secrets; scrub fixtures.
- CI runs migrations against Postgres+pgvector, `alembic check`, then `pytest` — keep tests green locally the same way when touching schema.
